  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner, has died following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. Lomas, who lived in Melton, Leicestershire, began raising money for charity after an accident in 2007 that left her paralyzed from the chest down. She made headlines for running the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days while wearing a bionic suit and lighting the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square. In 2016, she took part in the Great North Run while pregnant, again wearing a bionic suit, and completed the half marathon in five days after being denied a place on the Vitality London 10k."
